WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:05.190
This is Sakuragi Institute.

00:00:05.770 --> 00:00:09.280
Satoshi and Go now greet
their first morning here.

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:17.830
Satoshi, it's morning.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.250
Wake up...

00:00:21.250 --> 00:00:22.870
You too, Go...

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:41.640
Oh, it's just Barrierd.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.020
We can eat as much as we like?!

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:50.270
Of course! After all, we're...

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:54.030
...research fellows here!

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:55.860
Being research fellows is amazing!

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:57.530
Yeah!

00:00:57.530 --> 00:00:59.530
They've got Pokémon food, too!

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:04.540
So, I was considering
using Electroweb,

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:07.790
but I figured I really ought to
go with 100,000 Volts instead!

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:09.000
Right, Pikachu?

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:13.840
Director Sakuragi!

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:15.050
Good morning.

00:01:15.050 --> 00:01:16.590
Good morning!

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:17.930
Morning, Koharu.

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:18.550
Good morning.

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:23.680
Did you sleep well?

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.060
Perfectly!

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:28.020
You even have a food corner...
This is the best!

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:30.400
Satoshi's been stuffing his face
since he got here!

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.690
Yeah, stuffing my face since...
Wait, so have you!

00:01:33.690 --> 00:01:35.320
I guess.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:38.320
Wanpachi, I'll put your food
and water here.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:42.580
See you later.

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:44.370
Sure. Take care.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:46.620
You should eat with us, too.

00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:50.330
I already ate.
And I don't want to be late for school.

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:52.340
Well, see you later.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:54.670
I'll go!

00:01:54.670 --> 00:01:56.220
Me, too!

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:03.310
I'm so sorry!

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:07.430
The bus got stuck in traffic...

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:12.770
Oh, that's right.
I hadn't introduced you yet.

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:14.900
I'm Renji, an assistant here.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:17.150
And my other assistant...

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:18.490
I'm Kikuna.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:21.700
The cause of the traffic jam
is up on the news sites.

00:02:25.240 --> 00:02:26.580
Fushigisou!

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:31.210
A city-wide outbreak of Fushigisou?

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:34.750
Fushigidane. Fushigisou.
Fushigibana.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:39.800
mystery
True to the "fushigi" in their names,
they're full of mysteries.

00:02:39.800 --> 00:02:41.340
Let's go investigate!

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:45.140
This'll be our first job as research fellows
at the Sakuragi Institute!

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:47.810
Yeah! Let's give it
all we've got, Pikachu!

00:02:48.890 --> 00:02:52.440
By the way, Satoshi,
do you have a smartphone?

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:53.690
Smartphone?

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:55.070
Have this, then.

00:02:55.070 --> 00:02:56.650
Thank you!

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:58.780
Go, you take out yours.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:00.030
All right.

00:03:03.620 --> 00:03:05.120
Rotom!

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:08.290
Raise up your smartphones,
both of you.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:09.710
All right!

00:03:11.830 --> 00:03:13.210
It went in...

00:03:14.710 --> 00:03:15.670
What's this?

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:21.300
It's called a Smartphone Rotom.

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.970
It's got Pokémon Index
functions, as well.

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:25.050
Thank you, Sir!

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:26.220
Right, now...

00:03:27.010 --> 00:03:28.850
Let's go!

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:40.490
Hey, you still not ready? C'mon, hurry up!

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:43.070
You all packed and ready to leave?

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:45.780
I'll show you this wide mysterious world

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:48.660
And skip the slow send-off

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.000
Be it through fire or through water

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.670
I'm fumbling blindly through the days

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:58.170
When I don't even know what the next second will bring

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:03.430
Each and every one of my memories

00:04:03.430 --> 00:04:08.010
Can always be found inside a Ball

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.930
On 1, 2, 3, dive in!

00:04:11.930 --> 00:04:17.690
I've got the future plans I imagined in my pocket

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:24.700
Greeting someone new is always fresh

00:04:24.700 --> 00:04:28.780
No need (No need!) to hesitate! Try! (Try!)

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:30.240
Let's have a fight!

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:32.960
1: Once the battle's done

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:34.790
2: And we're laughing or crying

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:39.130
On 3, let's be friends!

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:45.800
Any day and every day, that's always been my rule

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:51.140
With this unpredictable, boundless world awaiting

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:53.640
Let's go! Every time you trip and fall

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:57.770
Let's go! You pick yourself up by my side

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.440
I choose you!

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:08.450
Fushigisou!
The Oh-<i>Sou</i> Mysterious

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:14.290
I ask of you: what is Team Rocket?

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:18.920
An evil organization spearheading
the Pokémon world, now and forever.

00:05:18.920 --> 00:05:20.670
What evil do we commit?

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:24.670
Steal each and every
strong or rare Pokémon.

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.550
To what end?

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:30.890
To create the mightiest Pokémon army
using the Pokémon we stole.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:38.400
For that purpose, I have prepared
the ultimate secret weapon.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:42.440
Go! Make the whole world learn to fear
the name of Team Rocket!

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:46.070
<i>Your wish is our command,
Sakaki, Sir!</i>

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:52.990
That's weird...

00:05:52.990 --> 00:05:56.040
It should be around here...

00:05:58.420 --> 00:06:00.420
Please stop!

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:01.210
Over there!

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:04.210
Miss Junsa!

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.260
Did something happen?

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:07.800
As you can see...

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:10.930
Fushigisou!

00:06:13.810 --> 00:06:17.520
Fushigisou! Seed Pokémon!
Grass/Poison type!

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:21.400
Exposure to sunlight
adds to its strength!

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:24.270
Sunlight also makes the bud
on its back grow larger!

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:27.610
I wonder where
the Fushigisou are going.

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:30.410
Oh, that's right.

00:06:30.410 --> 00:06:33.530
This might not have anything
to do with the Fushigisou,

00:06:33.530 --> 00:06:34.410
but look at this.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:36.660
Team Rocket?!

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:38.870
I've read about them online.

00:06:38.870 --> 00:06:42.080
Apparently they're bad guys who
steal people's Pokémon...

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:44.840
But the bit about the talking Nyarth
has to be a lie, yeah?

00:06:44.840 --> 00:06:47.920
Most people <i>would</i> think so, huh?

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:52.930
We're on guard because there were reports
they'd been sighted around here.

00:06:52.930 --> 00:06:54.640
You take care, too.

00:06:54.640 --> 00:06:55.510
All right!

00:06:58.480 --> 00:06:59.730
Pikachu!

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:04.230
What's wrong?

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:11.410
Seems like it wants to
keep moving, but can't.

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:12.610
Let's help it!

00:07:12.610 --> 00:07:13.410
Don't!

00:07:13.820 --> 00:07:15.160
Why?

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:19.330
We're here to investigate
the Fushigisou outbreak, yeah?

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:22.620
If we help them, we won't be able to
solve the mystery.

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:25.090
It's in trouble,
so we should help!

00:07:25.090 --> 00:07:28.510
It's a mistake to try and help
anyone and everyone!

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:32.130
If a Pokémon can't get through trouble on its own,
then that's the end of the line!

00:07:32.130 --> 00:07:33.720
What do you mean,
"end of the line"?!

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:36.760
If we helped it,
we'd rob it of its strength to live, yeah?!

00:07:36.760 --> 00:07:38.100
That doesn't make any sense!

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:40.430
If I want to help someone, I will!

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:42.770
Helping someone just on a whim...

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:46.360
...because you think they're cute,
or you feel bad for them, is just human conceit!

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:49.820
I don't care if it's conceit or whatever!
I'm helping it!

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:54.700
It's fine, I'll get you up.

00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:56.700
All right...

00:08:02.330 --> 00:08:03.620
Told you so.

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:05.380
Oh, leave me alone, will you?

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:07.380
Oh, I see how it is.

00:08:07.380 --> 00:08:10.590
Sheesh... Back with Lugia,
I accepted you as my friend,

00:08:10.590 --> 00:08:13.260
but it seems I misjudged you.

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:15.340
I don't need you to be my friend!

00:08:17.260 --> 00:08:19.470
So you're one of <i>those</i> guys, too...

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:21.730
You say something?

00:08:23.390 --> 00:08:26.650
Forget it!
I'll investigate on my own!

00:08:26.650 --> 00:08:29.440
Oh, will you now?
Well, suit yourself!

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:31.030
Yeah, I will!

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:46.040
All right! Me, too!

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:50.050
Don't copy me!

00:08:50.050 --> 00:08:51.630
Right back at you!

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:02.980
Rotom, what's that?

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:06.730
A Pokémon Gym under construction.

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:19.620
There's a sweet scent in the air...

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:25.580
I see!

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:28.420
The Fushigisou might be
going there to evolve.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:29.330
Evolve?

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:32.840
Them letting out a sweet scent
from their bud like that...

00:09:32.840 --> 00:09:36.510
...is a sign that they're about to evolve
and have their flowers bloom!

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:45.270
Pocket Monsters!

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:54.480
Grass
Poison
Fushigisou

00:10:01.410 --> 00:10:03.740
They keep coming
from that way, too.

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:06.290
There's Fushigidane, too!

00:10:06.790 --> 00:10:08.920
They're so cute!

00:10:09.750 --> 00:10:12.710
Rotom, do you have any info
on that place?

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:17.340
This is a photo from
when construction was starting!

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:19.720
Oh, Wanriky!

00:10:19.720 --> 00:10:23.430
Before construction began,
it was a sunny grassland!

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:30.980
Wild Fushigidane and Fushigisou
would gather there to bask in the sun!

00:10:40.950 --> 00:10:43.830
The Fushigisou are disappointed.

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:45.370
You can tell?

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:47.330
It's obvious from
the look on their faces!

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:49.540
I can't tell at all...

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:15.610
Are they climbing up,
since the sun shines brighter up top?

00:11:17.150 --> 00:11:18.530
Let's go, Pikachu!

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:24.450
You mean we'll know
if we go up there?

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:32.960
Awesome!

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:40.510
Grab on!

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:47.560
Easy does it...

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:52.140
Now up there, huh?

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:54.600
Get on.

00:11:55.230 --> 00:11:56.270
Are you sure?

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:57.360
Yeah.

00:11:57.860 --> 00:11:58.980
Thanks!

00:12:00.070 --> 00:12:02.860
And away we go!

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:05.820
Here.

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:26.050
We made it!

00:12:29.970 --> 00:12:31.930
They're all basking in the sun!

00:12:33.100 --> 00:12:36.980
The Fushigidane's bulbs are
taking in sunlight and growing bigger!

00:12:40.110 --> 00:12:41.860
What a sweet scent...

00:12:41.860 --> 00:12:46.910
Does this mean they really <i>did</i> come here
seeking stronger sunlight?

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:48.160
I know!

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:51.370
We might understand them better
if we become Fushigisou ourselves!

00:12:52.500 --> 00:12:54.160
That's it...

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:57.210
Pikachu, you be the bud.

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:02.130
I'm starting to feel like Fushigisou.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:04.510
This feels so nice...

00:13:09.390 --> 00:13:12.470
Oh, man...
It really <i>does</i> feel nice...

00:13:19.310 --> 00:13:21.320
The wind's so pleasant.

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:26.070
This spot is famous in Kuchiba
for its strong winds.

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:36.120
Is this evolution?

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:42.750
What's that?!

00:13:47.050 --> 00:13:49.140
If you ask us about "this" or "that"…

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:52.220
We'll answer out of
sympathy for the world!

00:13:53.720 --> 00:13:56.140
To protect the world from devastation.

00:13:56.140 --> 00:13:58.350
To preserve world peace.

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:02.150
Championing the evils
of truth and love.

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:04.860
We're the lovely, charming villains.

00:14:05.690 --> 00:14:06.610
Musashi!

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:07.570
Kojiro!

00:14:08.200 --> 00:14:11.070
The Team Rocket duo
soars through the galaxy!

00:14:11.070 --> 00:14:14.490
Like a white hole,
a white tomorrow awaits us!

00:14:15.700 --> 00:14:17.960
Just kidding, meow!

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:25.210
Team Rocket?!
It's my first time seeing them!

00:14:25.210 --> 00:14:27.420
Sure, pleasure meeting you, meow...

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:31.140
The Nyarth really <i>is</i> talking!

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:33.720
I don't mesh well with
people like that, meow...

00:14:33.720 --> 00:14:37.060
Give the Fushigisou back,
Team Rocket!

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:41.020
With so many of them gathered in one place,
it's like they're saying "Please steal us"!

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:43.230
And so, of course we will do just that!

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:44.730
Farewell, brat boy!

00:14:44.730 --> 00:14:46.030
Wait!

00:14:46.030 --> 00:14:47.320
"Brat boy"?

00:14:47.320 --> 00:14:49.780
Pikachu! Iron Tail!

00:14:56.660 --> 00:14:58.040
I'm glad you're all right!

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:01.120
How dare you take my Fushigisou!

00:15:01.120 --> 00:15:02.460
We're going down, Nyarth!

00:15:02.460 --> 00:15:03.540
Roger that!

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:08.840
You have some nerve,
you know that?!

00:15:17.270 --> 00:15:19.390
This is the secret weapon, meow?

00:15:19.390 --> 00:15:21.140
Looks like a vending machine to me.

00:15:21.140 --> 00:15:23.860
Well, then we'll have to put in a coin!

00:15:23.860 --> 00:15:25.860
But do we even have one?

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:27.110
We sure do!

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:28.230
Here goes!

00:15:29.570 --> 00:15:30.610
Rocket...

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:31.950
Vending...

00:15:31.950 --> 00:15:33.740
Secret!

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:40.710
So these Balls contain awesome Pokémon
that Sakaki picked out, huh?

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:43.000
Come on!

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:49.170
The Atrocious Pokémon, Gyarados!

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:52.550
The Armor Pokémon, Banguirus!

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:55.180
Way to go, Sakaki!

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:57.930
These are some energetic
and strong Pokémon!

00:15:57.930 --> 00:15:59.020
Commence attack, meow!

00:15:59.430 --> 00:16:01.060
Gyarados, go!

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:02.520
Banguirus, use Fire Fang!

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:06.560
Dodge it, Pikachu!

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:10.400
Something powerful!

00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:12.740
Evil Pulse!

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:15.490
Electroweb!

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:21.660
Lightning Speed!

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:28.460
Good!

00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:29.250
Awesome...

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:30.510
Another!

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:36.760
Pikachu!

00:16:36.760 --> 00:16:38.760
Stone Edge!

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:46.730
This doesn't look good!

00:16:46.730 --> 00:16:47.560
I know that!

00:16:47.560 --> 00:16:49.650
Pikachu, are you all right?

00:16:52.860 --> 00:16:54.780
Let's finish them
with a team attack!

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:55.610
Yeah!

00:17:02.330 --> 00:17:03.960
Solar Beam?

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:06.920
Thank you, everyone!

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:13.170
Hey, Gyarados, are you okay?

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:15.130
Can you go on, Banguirus?

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:21.010
Well then, let's dish out some pain
on the Fushigisou first!

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:22.680
And <i>then</i> we'll catch them!

00:17:22.680 --> 00:17:23.810
Destroyer Beam!

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:31.520
I won't let you!

00:17:45.120 --> 00:17:48.000
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:56.970
Go!

00:18:10.610 --> 00:18:12.730
That Pikachu really is incredible.

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:14.780
So we'd better stick to
our original plan.

00:18:15.240 --> 00:18:17.740
We <i>will</i> get
that Pikachu, meow!

00:18:20.700 --> 00:18:22.620
But now we're blasting off...

00:18:23.450 --> 00:18:26.540
<i>What an awful feeling!</i>

00:18:38.090 --> 00:18:40.090
They've started evolving!

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:49.310
Fushigibana!

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:56.650
Fushigibana. Seed Pokémon.
Grass/Poison type.

00:18:56.650 --> 00:19:01.490
Its flower is said to take on vivid colors
if it gets plenty of nutrition and sunlight.

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:04.620
The flower's aroma
soothes the emotions of people.

00:19:48.700 --> 00:19:53.670
The Fushigibana came here to
use the wind to spread their pollen!

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:58.210
Yeah. I guess this is the "strength to live"
you were talking about?

00:19:58.760 --> 00:20:00.720
Pokémon really are awesome!

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:04.970
Yeah, they sure are.

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:08.100
As are the two of you, though.

00:20:09.810 --> 00:20:11.600
No, never mind.

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:22.030
The mysterious strength hidden
in Fushigibana's pollen...

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:23.780
Another grand discovery!

00:20:23.780 --> 00:20:27.080
Well, when up against
the ultimate duo of Satoshi and I,

00:20:27.080 --> 00:20:29.200
it was an easy job!

00:20:29.200 --> 00:20:30.870
Today was a lot of fun!

00:20:30.870 --> 00:20:32.750
We got to see
the moment they evolved,

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:34.830
and became friends with
the Fushigisou!

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:38.540
First it was Lugia,
now Fushigisou...

00:20:38.540 --> 00:20:39.880
That's great, Satoshi.

00:20:39.880 --> 00:20:40.840
Yeah!

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:46.050
Well, then... While you're at it...

00:20:46.050 --> 00:20:47.220
Could you be <i>my</i> friend-

00:20:47.220 --> 00:20:50.220
What are you talking about?
We're already friends, right?

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:54.140
Oh, of course!

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:00.150
I'm home.

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:02.530
Welcome home.
What took you so long?

00:21:02.530 --> 00:21:05.740
All the flowers at the school
bloomed at once...

00:21:05.740 --> 00:21:08.950
I was in charge of cleanup...
It was <i>so</i> much work!

00:21:12.950 --> 00:21:15.210
What's with you?
How creepy...

00:21:15.210 --> 00:21:19.130
In any case,
my exceptional research fellows...

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:22.210
...have solved the mystery of
the Fushigisou march.

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:23.260
Thank you!

00:21:23.260 --> 00:21:26.050
We can still keep going!

00:21:26.050 --> 00:21:30.180
Yeah! I can't wait to see
what adventure lies in store next!

00:21:31.810 --> 00:21:36.140
Learning a new fact about Fushigisou
has allowed Satoshi and Go to make up.

00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:40.730
Tomorrow, more dreams and adventures await
in the world of Pocket Monsters!

